WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.042
A digit has a different value in each place: hundreds, thousands, ten thousands,

00:00:05.042 --> 00:00:09.139
hundred thousands and millions. Multiply the digit by its place value.

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:20.716
In 174,769, what value does the digit in the 100,000 place column represent? The

00:00:20.716 --> 00:00:26.867
answer is 100,000. 1 times 100,000 equals 100,000.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:35.297
A pupil at a market stall removes the contribution of the 1,000s digit from 938,988.

00:00:35.297 --> 00:00:39.348
What number remains? Pause the video and think.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:52.133
A pupil at a market stall removes the contribution of the 1,000s digit from 938,988.

00:00:52.133 --> 00:01:01.679
What number remains? The answer is 930,988. Without the 1,000s contribution, 938,988

00:01:01.679 --> 00:01:04.861
minus 8,000 equals 930,988.
